  "id": "shenjing-shuairuo",
  "term": "shenjing shuairuo",
  "definition": "Shenjing shuairuo refers to neurasthenia, a clinical idiom of distress described here as involving passive, fatigue-centered bodily complaints. In this source, it is contrasted with later adolescent self-harm as an earlier way distress was commonly expressed in China.",
